          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "I've finished the review and saved it in Project 02's reviews folder as `01_ROUND_ONE_CROSS_MODEL_REVIEW_CLAUDE_20261017.md`. Its supporting computations are in `numerics/round-1/claude-review/`, and a copy of the review is in the RH4 project docs.\n\n- **Correctness:** I found no mathematical error in round one. Every record replays, but two only with the 45-second time limit raised, because my machine is slower. The tail run also trips its 512-MiB memory check here (it used 564 MiB), though all its mathematical results match.\n- **Main new point:** I propose an activation lemma that would close the open finite range (690,989 ≤ N < 3,840,000) with about 20 certified rows instead of a full producer run. If it holds, the bound Λ ≤ 0.1745354 follows, conditional on the results the manuscript imports. The lemma is my own proof sketch and Codex should check it before it's used.\n\nThis session's chat record is saved in the project's `chat-histories/claude-cowork` folder, and the recorder reported no gaps. Nothing has been committed to git."
            ]
